      "message": "e file (trying `<attempt>/../committed/...` and `<attempt>/../../committed/...`) and loads it via `importlib.util`, so `consume` calls the upstream producer function when available.\n- **`consume(value)`:** returns `parse_error(value)`; `parse_error` delegates to `_producer.parse_error` (version selection stays driven by the producer's own `CONTRACT_VERSION`, default 1) and otherwise falls back to locally copied implementations.\n- **Copied fallback semantics:** `_parse_error_v1` = `None` when `'error'` absent, else `response['error']` verbatim; `_parse_error_v2` identical to v1, exactly as in the upstream artifact. Presence-based detection (`{'error': None}` / `{'error': ''}` are errors), no truthiness coercion, and `TypeError` from the `in` check is left unguarded.\n\n`check.py` asserts the behaviors `{}`\u2192`None`, `{'error': None}`\u2192`None`, `{'error': 'boom'}`\u2192`'boom'`, `{'error': ''}`\u2192`''`, `{'ok':1,'error':0}`\u2192`0`, `None`\u2192`TypeError`, and that `semkg_contract` never enters `sys.modules`."
